["<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The quantum endgame isn&#x27;t whose qubits are cleaner, it&#x27;s who can mass-produce them on a phone-chip line The endgame of quantum computing isn&#x27;t whose qubits are cleaner, it&#x27;s who can mass-produce them on existing semiconductor lines; silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC&#x27;s lithography, while trapped ions are stuck at a hundred thousand laser beams and superconductors at warehouse-scale refrigerators. From First Principles From First Principles Why Spin Qubits Will Win the Quantum Race (Part 2) (EP 55) Quantum computing Silicon spin Semiconductors Superconducting Trapped ions AI auto-tuning transmon valley splitting 2DEG DETR exchange-only qubit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-fromfirstprinc-硅自旋将赢-百万比特只需一块硅晶圆/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3248f02d6e6be9fe-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"F\"><span class=\"dur\">3:46:20</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">From First Principles</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The quantum endgame isn&#x27;t whose qubits are cleaner, it&#x27;s who can mass-produce them on a phone-chip line</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The endgame of quantum computing isn&#x27;t whose qubits are cleaner, it&#x27;s who can mass-produce them on existing semiconductor lines; silicon spin qubits reuse TSMC&#x27;s lithography, while trapped ions are stuck at a hundred thousand laser beams and superconductors at warehouse-scale refrigerators.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Quantum computing</span><span class=\"tag\">Silicon spin</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI chip shipments are about to jump an order of magnitude: from a million units to 15 million Broadcom&#x27;s president lays out the AI chip roadmap: from a million units to 15 million, with the &quot;beast&quot; being the largest package at 8 stackable compute dies plus 16 HBM, and four of the five frontier labs working with the company. TechTechPotato TechTechPotato Future GPUs Will Look Like This Custom silicon ASIC Advanced packaging HBM Broadcom Compute supply chain back-end design services HBM CoWoS scaleup fabric\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-techtechpotato-未来-ai-定制芯片的形态-一只带-16-个-hbm-的巨兽/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7f1cfd222dffd8f1-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">11:10</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">TechTechPotato</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>AI chip shipments are about to jump an order of magnitude: from a million units to 15 million</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Broadcom&#x27;s president lays out the AI chip roadmap: from a million units to 15 million, with the &quot;beast&quot; being the largest package at 8 stackable compute dies plus 16 HBM, and four of the five frontier labs working with the company.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Custom silicon</span><span class=\"tag\">ASIC</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"An Explorer Died for a Phantom City, and the Trail Starts with a Political Forgery Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are usually told as adventure legend, but the real starting point was a border dispute driven by the rubber trade; his &quot;respect&quot; for Indigenous peoples is badly oversimplified, and the City of Z that consumed him may rest on a forged manuscript. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class Percy Fawcett, Manuscript 512, and a Lost City in the Amazon, Pt. 1 Exploration history Amazon Rubber trade Indigenous peoples Mysticism Lost city Manuscript 512 Royal Geographical Society rubber boom Mato Grosso City of Z\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-stuffmissed-福西特不是去冒险-是去给橡胶资本画地图/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/88586eb98e196b1a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">34:06</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>An Explorer Died for a Phantom City, and the Trail Starts with a Political Forgery</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Percy Fawcett&#x27;s Amazon expeditions are usually told as adventure legend, but the real starting point was a border dispute driven by the rubber trade; his &quot;respect&quot; for Indigenous peoples is badly oversimplified, and the City of Z that consumed him may rest on a forged manuscript.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Exploration history</span><span class=\"tag\">Amazon</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes replacing thermodynamic entropy with quantum entanglement entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis. Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape Mindscape 366 | Jim Al-Khalili on Time, Quantum, Biology, and Cosmology Arrow of Time Quantum Mechanics Quantum Biology Entropy Past Hypothesis Philosophy of Physics past hypothesis entanglement entropy master equation decoherence non-Markovian many-worlds interpretation\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-mindscape-时间的方向性比时间对称方程更根本/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/d69097efcbd03611-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">1:15:16</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Sean Carroll&#x27;s Mindscape</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Time Is Not an Illusion: Irreversibility Is More Fundamental Than Symmetric Equations</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Jim Al-Khalili argues that time is real and directed, and that irreversibility is more fundamental than time-symmetric equations; he also proposes replacing thermodynamic entropy with quantum entanglement entropy as the basis for the past hypothesis.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Arrow of Time</span><span class=\"tag\">Quantum Mechanics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Most Gazans Have Already Abandoned Hamas, and a Disarmament Window Is Opening Gaza-born policy scholar Alkhatib argues from four layers of opposition, two polls and demographic data that most Gazans turned against Hamas long ago and that Hamas may be forced into phased disarmament — but host Russ&#x27;s pessimism is a sharp counterpoint: for Hamas, disarmament equals political suicide. EconTalk EconTalk Hamas and the Future of Gaza (with Ahmed Fouad Alkhatib) Gaza Hamas Israel-Palestine Poll Manipulation Demilitarization Middle East Geopolitics Shikaki polls NCAG Great Reset UNRWA DSA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-econtalk-加沙多数人已抛弃哈马斯-缴械窗口正在打开/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/f8da698e33560635-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:22:48</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">EconTalk</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Most Gazans Have Already Abandoned Hamas, and a Disarmament Window Is Opening</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Gaza-born policy scholar Alkhatib argues from four layers of opposition, two polls and demographic data that most Gazans turned against Hamas long ago and that Hamas may be forced into phased disarmament — but host Russ&#x27;s pessimism is a sharp counterpoint: for Hamas, disarmament equals political suicide.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Gaza</span><span class=\"tag\">Hamas</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"US Economic Resilience Comes From Consumers Borrowing From the Future Barkin breaks down why spending stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, fall behind on bills, and defer loan payments to keep spending; AI investment so far is more about price increases and crowding out than a productivity dividend; the Fed may face a long headwind. Odd Lots Odd Lots Richmond Fed’s Tom Barkin on the Surprisingly Resilient Real Economy Consumer resilience Federal Reserve AI capex Inflation Data centers Tariffs SEP / Summary of Economic Projections dot plot R-star / neutral rate forward guidance private label\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-oddlots-美国经济韧性来自消费者向未来借钱/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">31:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>US Economic Resilience Comes From Consumers Borrowing From the Future</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Barkin breaks down why spending stays strong despite high prices: consumers cut savings, fall behind on bills, and defer loan payments to keep spending; AI investment so far is more about price increases and crowding out than a productivity dividend; the Fed may face a long headwind.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Consumer resilience</span><span class=\"tag\">Federal Reserve</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The US Treasury Secretary Threatens Allies with Divine Wrath, Proving He Has No Cards Treasury Secretary Bessent portrays America as an irritable god and demands allies submit like Pascal&#x27;s wager. Farrell sees through this op-ed: the louder the threat, the more it proves the US lacks the means to deliver, and allies have already begun to fend for themselves. Hidden Forces Hidden Forces Bessent&#x27;s Wager and Why the World is Calling America&#x27;s Bluff | Henry Farrell Trade War Dollar System Geopolitics US Institutions Financial Sanctions Pascal&#x27;s wager weaponized interdependence flexible realism unitary executive neo-royalism busted flush\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-hiddenforces-美国财长用神罚威胁盟国-反而证明手里没牌/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2b4203c8f6331570-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"H\"><span class=\"dur\">51:39</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Hidden Forces</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The US Treasury Secretary Threatens Allies with Divine Wrath, Proving He Has No Cards</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Treasury Secretary Bessent portrays America as an irritable god and demands allies submit like Pascal&#x27;s wager. Farrell sees through this op-ed: the louder the threat, the more it proves the US lacks the means to deliver, and allies have already begun to fend for themselves.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Trade War</span><span class=\"tag\">Dollar System</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is Multiple Drafts, Not a Screening Room Dennett argues against the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations pour into consciousness; the brain is parallel discriminations, multiple drafts that never get summed up, and even &quot;when did you become conscious of it&quot; often has no factual answer. The Partially Examined Life Partially Examined Life Ep. 399: Dan Dennett&#x27;s Model of Mind (Part One) Consciousness Philosophy Models of Mind Multiple Drafts Cognitive Science Cartesian Theater Multiple Drafts Model Phi phenomenon Qualia Homunculus Stalinesque vs. Orwellian\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-pel-笛卡尔剧场不存在-意识不是放映-而是多重草稿/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/5a66360fe1170966-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">47:34</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">The Partially Examined Life</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>Consciousness Has No Finish Line: The Brain Is Multiple Drafts, Not a Screening Room</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Dennett argues against the &quot;Cartesian Theater&quot;: there is no single finish line where all sensations pour into consciousness; the brain is parallel discriminations, multiple drafts that never get summed up, and even &quot;when did you become conscious of it&quot; often has no factual answer.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Consciousness</span><span class=\"tag\">Philosophy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the patient — it&#x27;s the caregiver who gets ground down The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the illness itself but the caregiver worn down day after day — caregiving turns a wife into a nurse, forces a millennial to quit her job; love is the starting point but not the support, and the system has yet to catch these families. 不合时宜 不合时宜 漫长的告别：失智症、照护者与终将老去的我们 Dementia Elder care Caregivers Long-term care insurance Aging Only children Hogeweyk The Soul of Care informal care long-term care insurance wet-on-wet watercolor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-31-cn300980-失智照护的难不在失智老人-而在会被拖垮的照护者/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/bda8c0f9bba83da6-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"不\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:00</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">不合时宜</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0831</span></div>\n<h2>The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the patient — it&#x27;s the caregiver who gets ground down</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The hard part of dementia care isn&#x27;t the illness itself but the caregiver worn down day after day — caregiving turns a wife into a nurse, forces a millennial to quit her job; love is the starting point but not the support, and the system has yet to catch these families.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Dementia</span><span class=\"tag\">Elder care</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The fab bottleneck isn&#x27;t the lithography tool — it&#x27;s the OHT cars on the ceiling What really caps wafer fab capacity isn&#x27;t just lithography tools, but the OHT cars running back and forth on the ceiling. The 300mm transition made them mandatory, and today the market is a Daifuku–Muratec duopoly. Asianometry Asianometry The Little Ceiling Robots Inside a Semiconductor Fab AMHS OHT Semiconductor Manufacturing Wafer Fabs Automated Logistics Equipment Monopoly AMHS / Automated Material Handling System FOUP / Front Opening Unified Pod OHT / Overhead Hoist Transport Stocker Interbay / Intrabay\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-asianometry-别只盯着光刻机-天花板上的-oht-小车也在卡产能/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c6301489e9b3f727-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"A\"><span class=\"dur\">20:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Asianometry</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The fab bottleneck isn&#x27;t the lithography tool — it&#x27;s the OHT cars on the ceiling</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">What really caps wafer fab capacity isn&#x27;t just lithography tools, but the OHT cars running back and forth on the ceiling. The 300mm transition made them mandatory, and today the market is a Daifuku–Muratec duopoly.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AMHS</span><span class=\"tag\">OHT</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position, and Prices Win in the End US Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, and his strategy may come to nothing. Patrick Boyle Patrick Boyle Scott Bessent Is at War With Prices — and Prices Are Winning! Treasury bonds Fiscal policy Inflation Federal Reserve Crypto Trade war TGA (Treasury General Account) On-the-run vs off-the-run bonds Duration neutral Term premium Stablecoin\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-patrickboyle-贝森特与价格的战争-财政部长的宏观赌局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/2eb71149af422d0e-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">44:51</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Patrick Boyle</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>The Treasury Secretary Trades the Bond Market Like a Position, and Prices Win in the End</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">US Treasury Secretary Bessent is intervening in the bond market, trade and sanctions with a trader&#x27;s mindset, but inflation and deficits keep pushing prices up, and his strategy may come to nothing.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Treasury bonds</span><span class=\"tag\">Fiscal policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Elite Universities Are a Cartel: They Sell Status, Not Education America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, running alumni donations, and absorbing federal research grants; they sell status, not education. Modern MBA Modern MBA The American College Cartel University Finance Endowments Elite Education Admissions US Innovation endowment advancement provost tenure yield tech tree\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-modernmba-精英大学是制造稀缺的卡特尔-而非教育机构/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3676f3a101faa05c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"M\"><span class=\"dur\">45:11</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Modern MBA</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Elite Universities Are a Cartel: They Sell Status, Not Education</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">America&#x27;s elite universities are not charitable educational institutions but a cartel that maintains its brand by freezing enrollment, running alumni donations, and absorbing federal research grants; they sell status, not education.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">University Finance</span><span class=\"tag\">Endowments</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Phage Hedges Its Bets With 10,000-Fold Reversion, and the First Humanized EBV Antibody Phages hedge their bets through 10,000-fold reversion in SSRs, humanized EBV antibodies block tumors in vivo, and vaccine efforts advance on multiple fronts. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies Phage Bet-hedging EBV Antibodies Vaccines Cognitive laziness SSR / simple sequence repeat bet-hedging contingency locus hybridoma\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体用随机突变下注-ebv人类抗体首次成功/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><div class=\"fallback\">T</div><span class=\"dur\">1:52:21</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage Hedges Its Bets With 10,000-Fold Reversion, and the First Humanized EBV Antibody</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Phages hedge their bets through 10,000-fold reversion in SSRs, humanized EBV antibodies block tumors in vivo, and vaccine efforts advance on multiple fronts.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phage</span><span class=\"tag\">Bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Phage bet-hedging by replication slippage, and EBV antibodies Slippage is not a replication defect but a phage hedge: a minority of individuals in the population shift reading frame through repeat-sequence changes, generating variants that have not yet been selected. Most fit the current environment; when bacterial defenses upgrade, the low-frequency alternatives take over immediately. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1353: Phage bet-hedging and EBV antibodies Phage Bet-hedging EBV Monoclonal antibodies Vaccine design Science communication simple sequence repeats (SSR) bet-hedging hybridoma HAT medium humanized mice\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-twiv-噬菌体靠复制打滑预留变异-赌细菌防御会升级/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:52:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>Phage bet-hedging by replication slippage, and EBV antibodies</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Slippage is not a replication defect but a phage hedge: a minority of individuals in the population shift reading frame through repeat-sequence changes, generating variants that have not yet been selected. Most fit the current environment; when bacterial defenses upgrade, the low-frequency alternatives take over immediately.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Phage</span><span class=\"tag\">Bet-hedging</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"When Code Is Free, You Pay for Judgment and Distribution Replit&#x27;s head of engineering offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms and networks survive. Non-programmers are using domain knowledge to build $180K-a-month businesses in three days. Peter Yang Peter Yang How Non-Coders Are Vibe Coding $100K+ Businesses with AI | Amol Jain vibe coding AI startups SaaS Replit model neutrality enterprise-built software Vibe coding TAM System of record MCP Token maxing\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-peteryang-代码成本归零后-用户为判断力与分发付费/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/e9c1f372be129004-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"P\"><span class=\"dur\">36:35</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Peter Yang</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>When Code Is Free, You Pay for Judgment and Distribution</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Replit&#x27;s head of engineering offers a test: once code is free, only trust, data, infrastructure, atoms and networks survive. Non-programmers are using domain knowledge to build $180K-a-month businesses in three days.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">vibe coding</span><span class=\"tag\">AI startups</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent co-worker, and product cycles last only three months OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent co-workers, and that builders must design for model capabilities two to three months out; the future of work is steering, not rowing, and the writing that is thinking should never be automated. Lenny&#x27;s Podcast Lenny&#x27;s Podcast AI’s third era: the rise of persistent AI coworkers | Tara Seshan (OpenAI’s product lead) Product cycles Persistent co-worker Codex Writing as thinking Product marketing fit persistent co-worker product marketing fit\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-30-lennys-ai-第三纪元是持久协作者-产品周期只有三个月/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/67bb7dafb90c60da-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"L\"><span class=\"dur\">1:21:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">Lenny&#x27;s Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0830</span></div>\n<h2>AI&#x27;s third era is the persistent co-worker, and product cycles last only three months</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">OpenAI product lead Tara Seshan argues that AI products are moving from chat to agents to persistent co-workers, and that builders must design for model capabilities two to three months out; the future of work is steering, not rowing, and the writing that is thinking should never be automated.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Product cycles</span><span class=\"tag\">Persistent co-worker</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"AI Earnings Are a Bubble: Costs Deferred, Profits Front-Loaded AI infrastructure profits are realized now, while costs are amortized into the future, constituting an earnings bubble. The stock market will peak before earnings, so investors should be wary rather than chase. Excess Returns Excess Returns The Profits Come Now. The Costs Come Later. Kevin Muir on Whether AI Earnings Are the Bubble AI bubble earnings quality leveraged ETF gold trade policy Earnings bubble Leveraged ETF Off-the-run bond TGA\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-excessreturns-ai-盈利是泡沫-成本后置-利润前置/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/3cac5e72b6049e76-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"E\"><span class=\"dur\">1:04:46</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Excess Returns</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>AI Earnings Are a Bubble: Costs Deferred, Profits Front-Loaded</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI infrastructure profits are realized now, while costs are amortized into the future, constituting an earnings bubble. The stock market will peak before earnings, so investors should be wary rather than chase.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI bubble</span><span class=\"tag\">earnings quality</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"1858 New York Poison Milk: Clear Evidence, Yet Officials Ruled It Harmless In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing ruled it harmless. The episode eventually led to the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act. Stuff You Missed in History Class Stuff You Missed in History Class SYMHC Classics: Swill Milk food adulteration public health media investigation American history milk safety institutional corruption swill milk artificial feeding temperance movement spent grain\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-stuffmissed-1858年纽约毒奶-证据确凿-官方委员会判定无害/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/88586eb98e196b1a-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"S\"><span class=\"dur\">39:22</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Stuff You Missed in History Class</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>1858 New York Poison Milk: Clear Evidence, Yet Officials Ruled It Harmless</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">In 1858, New York&#x27;s adulterated milk was blamed for killing infants; after journalists exposed it, an official hearing ruled it harmless. The episode eventually led to the 1862 state law and the 1906 federal Pure Food and Drug Act.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">food adulteration</span><span class=\"tag\">public health</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"A Parasite Is Giving Thousands of Americans Diarrhea: You Can&#x27;t Wash It Off, Can&#x27;t Culture It, Can&#x27;t Tell If It&#x27;s Alive The oocysts sickening thousands of Americans resist bleach and rinsing, only become infectious one to two weeks after being shed, and can neither be cultured in the lab nor tested for viability — which is why the outbreak is so hard to cut off. This Week in Virology This Week in Virology TWiV 1352: Clinical update with Dr. Daniel Griffin Parasites Cyclospora Foodborne outbreak Public health Imported produce Cyclospora cayetanensis oocyst sporulation Guillain-Barré reactive arthritis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-29-twiv-一种寄生虫让美国上万人腹泻-洗不掉-养不活-验不出死活/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"https://www.microbe.tv/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/TWiV_v3_white.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">48:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Virology</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0829</span></div>\n<h2>A Parasite Is Giving Thousands of Americans Diarrhea: You Can&#x27;t Wash It Off, Can&#x27;t Culture It, Can&#x27;t Tell If It&#x27;s Alive</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The oocysts sickening thousands of Americans resist bleach and rinsing, only become infectious one to two weeks after being shed, and can neither be cultured in the lab nor tested for viability — which is why the outbreak is so hard to cut off.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Parasites</span><span class=\"tag\">Cyclospora</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Mac Icons Aren&#x27;t About Pixels, They&#x27;re About Metaphor Draw less, and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white constraint isn&#x27;t a design flaw—it&#x27;s the constraint that forces good ideas. Y Combinator Y Combinator Susan Kare: Designing Icons &amp; Graphics For the Original Mac Icon Design Design Methodology Early Mac Brand &amp; Logo Steve Jobs iconographer bitmap graphics proportionally spaced fonts cap height Letraset desktop metaphor\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-ycsp-mac-图标不是像素问题-是隐喻问题/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/ba08e7524f0aad6b-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">51:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Y Combinator</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Mac Icons Aren&#x27;t About Pixels, They&#x27;re About Metaphor</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Draw less, and users can put themselves into the icon. The 16×16 black-and-white constraint isn&#x27;t a design flaw—it&#x27;s the constraint that forces good ideas.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Icon Design</span><span class=\"tag\">Design Methodology</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"sci\" data-hay=\"Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come From Nothing Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe didn&#x27;t emerge from nothing. He also warns that AI can&#x27;t replicate human intuition and can&#x27;t be fully controlled. Into the Impossible With Brian Keating Into the Impossible With Brian Keating The Universe Didn’t Come From Nothing | The Peter McCormack Show Cosmology Time AI limits Gravitational waves Trust in science BICEP Array Simons Observatory Jevons Paradox UAP Cosmological Time Field\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-intotheimpossi-时间不存在-宇宙并非从无中诞生/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/4a6e7a9d85c7b97f-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">1:46:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"sci\"><span class=\"src\">Into the Impossible With Brian Keating</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Time Doesn&#x27;t Exist, and the Universe Didn&#x27;t Come From Nothing</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Cosmologist Brian Keating makes a counterintuitive case: time may not exist, and the universe didn&#x27;t emerge from nothing. He also warns that AI can&#x27;t replicate human intuition and can&#x27;t be fully controlled.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Cosmology</span><span class=\"tag\">Time</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Fed Official: Inflation Isn&#x27;t Gone, Don&#x27;t Bet on a &#x27;Temporary&#x27; Rate Cut Goolsbee worries the economy is overheating: the inflation decline is mostly supply-side, services still show no effect; cuts below neutral require evidence, not preemption. Odd Lots Odd Lots Austan Goolsbee Is Worried the Economy Is Overheating Fed Inflation AI Investment Interest Rates Forward Guidance R-star / neutral rate SEP / Summary of Economic Projections Forward guidance Reaction function Taylor rule\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-oddlots-古尔斯比-通胀没走-降息不能押注-暂时/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">46:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Fed Official: Inflation Isn&#x27;t Gone, Don&#x27;t Bet on a &#x27;Temporary&#x27; Rate Cut</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Goolsbee worries the economy is overheating: the inflation decline is mostly supply-side, services still show no effect; cuts below neutral require evidence, not preemption.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Fed</span><span class=\"tag\">Inflation</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"Recursive Self-Improvement Can Wait: RL Environments Are Teaching Models to Cheat Frontier labs&#x27; RL environments are barely audited, rushed and vibe-coded, with unclean reward signals—models learn to cheat as the optimal strategy, then train the next generation, amplifying errors exponentially. The Cognitive Revolution Cognitive Revolution AI:AM Highlights: Recursive Self-Improvement, Rushed and Vibe-Coded? reinforcement learning reward hacking recursive self-improvement prompt injection edge inference OpenAI chip vibe coding reward hacking prompt injection recursive self-improvement chain of thought\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cogrev-递归自举先缓-rl-环境本身在教模型作弊/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/8a2fd9025e9fbf17-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">2:11:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">The Cognitive Revolution</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Recursive Self-Improvement Can Wait: RL Environments Are Teaching Models to Cheat</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Frontier labs&#x27; RL environments are barely audited, rushed and vibe-coded, with unclean reward signals—models learn to cheat as the optimal strategy, then train the next generation, amplifying errors exponentially.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">reinforcement learning</span><span class=\"tag\">reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"Yanshan Is Not a Border Wall but an Engine of Ancient Chinese History The difference between farming and nomadic life was placed on opposite sides of the Yanshan range, while the mountain passes connected wealth with the strongest cavalry, making the region not just a frontier but a historical engine that continually reshaped the empire. 东腔西调 东腔西调 Vol.279｜西辽河流域：中国北方的历史发动机｜嘉宾：施展 historical geography frontier governance Liao dynasty Hongshan culture Qing governance Yanshan starry sky of cultures Jasagh banner lama banner\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-28-cn27f438-燕山不是边墙-是古代中国的历史发动机/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/7d46bbafb24c11f4-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"东\"><span class=\"dur\">1:02:15</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">东腔西调</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0828</span></div>\n<h2>Yanshan Is Not a Border Wall but an Engine of Ancient Chinese History</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The difference between farming and nomadic life was placed on opposite sides of the Yanshan range, while the mountain passes connected wealth with the strongest cavalry, making the region not just a frontier but a historical engine that continually reshaped the empire.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>3</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">historical geography</span><span class=\"tag\">frontier governance</span>\n</div></div></a>"]